<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Estimated Income Tax</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 10px; }
  td, th { padding: 5px; text-align: left; }
  .header-title { font-size: 24pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .sub-header { font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .section-title { font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 5px; }
  .label { font-weight: normal; }
  .value { font-weight: normal; }
  .small-text { font-size: 9pt; line-height: 1.3; }
  .two-column { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }
  .two-column > div { width: 48%; }
  .divider { border-top: 1px solid #000; margin: 20px 0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div>
      <div style="font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold;">Form 1041-ES</div>
      <div style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Estimated Income Tax for Estates and Trusts</div>
      <div style="font-size: 10pt;">OMB No. 15-045-0971</div>
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: right;">
      <div style="font-size: 24pt; font-weight: bold;">2006</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Purpose of Form</div>
  <div class="small-text">
    Use this package to figure and pay estimated tax for an estate or trust. Estimated tax is the amount of tax an estate or trust expects to owe for the year after subtracting the amount of any credits.
  </div>
  <div class="small-text" style="margin-top: 10px;">
    This package is primarily for first-time filers. If you are a repeat filer, please use the electronic Federal Tax Payment System (EFTPS) if you are, fiscally, did not use any prior year's estimated tax payments.
  </div>
  <div class="small-text" style="margin-top: 10px;">
    If the estate or trust is required to file an annual income tax return, you must use this package. However, do not use this package if the estate or trust is required to file an annual income tax return.
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Who Must Make Estimated Tax Payments</div>
  <div class="small-text">
    Generally, a fiduciary of an estate or trust must pay estimated tax if the estate or trust expects to owe more than <span data-field="threshold_amount_1">{{ threshold_amount_1 }}</span> in tax for the year.
  </div>
  <div class="small-text" style="margin-top: 10px;">
    The tax shown on the 2005 tax return (110%) of that amount if the estate or trust's adjusted gross income for 2005 was more than <span data-field="threshold_amount_2">{{ threshold_amount_2 }}</span>, and less than <span data-field="threshold_amount_3">{{ threshold_amount_3 }}</span>, or if the estate or trust's adjusted gross income for 2005 was more than <span data-field="threshold_amount_4">{{ threshold_amount_4 }}</span>.
  </div>
  <div class="small-text" style="margin-top: 10px;">
    However, if a return was not filed for 2005 or that return did not cover a full tax year, item 2 does not apply.
  </div>
  <div class="small-text" style="margin-top: 10px;">
    For this purpose, include household employment taxes when figuring the tax shown on the tax return, but only if:
  </div>
  <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 5px;">
    <li class="small-text">The estate or trust was required to make estimated tax payments to the IRS.</li>
    <li class="small-text">The estate or trust was required to make household employment taxes when figuring its estimated tax.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="section-title">Instructions for 2006 Estimated Tax Worksheet</div>
  <div class="small-text">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
      <div>
        <div style="font-weight: bold;">Line 4 - Exemption</div>
        <div class="small-text">
          Decedent's estates. A decedent's estate is allowed a <span data-field="exemption_amount">{{ exemption_amount }}</span> exemption.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="font-weight: bold;">Line 7 - Tax</div>
        <div class="small-text">
          Electing Alaska Native Settlement Trusts. Must multiply line 6 by <span data-field="multiplier_1">{{ multiplier_1 }}</span> to figure the estimated tax.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
      <div style="font-weight: bold;">Line 10 - Credits</div>
      <div class="small-text">
        For details on credits the estate or trust may claim, see the instructions for line 2, 3, and 4.
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
      <div style="font-weight: bold;">Line 12 - Other Taxes</div>
      <div class="small-text">
        Enter any other taxes such as:
        <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 5px;">
          <li class="small-text">Tax from recapture of investment credit.</li>
          <li class="small-text">Tax from qualified electric vehicle credit.</li>
          <li class="small-text">The Indian gaming tax.</li>
          <li class="small-text">Employer-provided child care facilities.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
      <div style="font-weight: bold;">Line 14 - Qualified Distributions</div>
      <div class="small-text">
        Qualified distributions. A qualified distribution is any distribution from a trust that is not subject to income tax.
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
      <div style="font-weight: bold;">Line 16 - Estimated Tax</div>
      <div class="small-text">
        Estimated tax.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <div class="section-title">Whereto to File</div>
  <div class="small-text">
    Mail the payment voucher to:
    <div style="font-weight: bold;">Internal Revenue Service</div>
    <div class="small-text">
      <span data-field="address_line_1">{{ address_line_1 }}</span><br>
      <span data-field="city_state_zip">{{ city_state_zip }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Amending Estimated Tax Payments</div>
  <div class="small-text">
    To change or amend the estate's or trust's estimated payments, refer the instructions for the 2006 Estimated Tax Worksheet on page 3. Then use the worksheets under Change in Estimated Tax Payments.
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">When a Penalty Is Applied</div>
  <div class="small-text">
    In some cases, the estate or trust may owe a penalty if it files its return late.
  </div>

</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div>
      <div style="font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold;">Form 1041-ES</div>
      <div style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Estimated Income Tax for Estates and Trusts</div>
      <div style="font-size: 10pt;">OMB No. 15-045-0971</div>
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: right;">
      <div style="font-size: 24pt; font-weight: bold;">2006</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Estates, if the estate has adopted a calendar year as its tax year, file using the rules listed under Trusts above.</div>

  <div class="section-title">Electronic Deposits</div>
  <div class="small-text">
    A financial institution that maintains a Treasury Tax and Loan (TTAL) account, may be required to deposit the estate's or trust's estimated tax payments using the Electronic Federal Tax Payment System (EFTPS). The electronic deposit must be made by the last day of the month following the month in which the tax is due.
  </div>
  <div class="small-text" style="margin-top: 10px;">
    The fiduciary on behalf of a trust or trust's estate may use EFTPS on behalf of a trust and fails to do so, it may be subject to a <span data-field="penalty_description">{{ penalty_description }}</span>.
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Table 1: Estimated Tax Worksheet</div>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 10%;">Line</th>
        <th style="width: 30%;">Description</th>
        <th style="width: 20%;">Amount</th>
        <th style="width: 20%;">Tax Rate</th>
        <th style="width: 20%;">Tax Due</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>1</td>
        <td>Enter adjusted total income expected in 2006</td>
        <td><span data-field="table1_line1">{{ table1_line1 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>2</td>
        <td>Enter any expected income distribution deduction</td>
        <td><span data-field="table1_line2">{{ table1_line2 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>3</td>
        <td>Enter any estate tax deduction</td>
        <td><span data-field="table1_line3">{{ table1_line3 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>4</td>
        <td>Add lines 2 through 4</td>
        <td><span data-field="table1_line4">{{ table1_line4 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>5</td>
        <td>Taxable income of estate or trust. Subtract line 5 from line 1</td>
        <td><span data-field="table1_line5">{{ table1_line5 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>6</td>
        <td>Tax. Figure your tax on line 6 by using the 2006 Tax Rate Schedule below. If the estate or trust expects a net capital gain or qualified dividends and line 6 is more than zero, use the Tax Computation Worksheet Using Maximum Capital Gains Rates. See instructions for line 6.</td>
        <td><span data-field="table1_line6">{{ table1_line6 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>7</td>
        <td>Alternative minimum tax</td>
        <td><span data-field="table1_line7">{{ table1_line7 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>8</td>
        <td>Add lines 7 and 8. Include any tax on lump-sum distributions from Form 4972</td>
        <td><span data-field="table1_line8">{{ table1_line8 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>9</td>
        <td>Credits (see instructions)</td>
        <td><span data-field="table1_line9">{{ table1_line9 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>10</td>
        <td>Subtract line 10 from line 9. If zero or less, enter -0</td>
        <td><span data-field="table1_line10">{{ table1_line10 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>11</td>
        <td>Other taxes (see instructions)</td>
        <td><span data-field="table1_line11">{{ table1_line11 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>12</td>
        <td>Estimated tax. Add lines 11 and 12. Reduce this total by any credit you expect to claim on Form 4136 (see instructions).</td>
        <td><span data-field="table1_line12">{{ table1_line12 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>13</td>
        <td>Enter the tax shown on the 2005 Form 1041 (110% of that amount if the estate or trust's AGGI on that return was more than $150,000, and less than $3,000, or if the estate or trust's AGGI on that return was more than $3,000).</td>
        <td><span data-field="table1_line13">{{ table1_line13 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>14</td>
        <td>Income tax withheld and estimated to be withheld during 2006 and other refundable credits.</td>
        <td><span data-field="table1_line14">{{ table1_line14 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>15</td>
        <td>Subtract line 15 from line 14.</td>
        <td><span data-field="table1_line15">{{ table1_line15 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>16</td>
        <td>Estimated amount. If line 13 minus line 15 is less than $1,000, the estate or trust is not required to make estimated tax payments. If line 13 minus line 15 is more than $1,000, the estate or trust must make estimated tax payments.</td>
        <td><span data-field="table1_line16">{{ table1_line16 }}</span></td>
        <td></td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="section-title" style="margin-top: 30px;">2006 Tax Rate Schedule</div>
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <table style="font-size: 10pt;">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th style="width: 30%;">Over</th>
            <th style="width: 30%;">Taxable Income</th>
            <th style="width: 40%;">The tax is:</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>0</td>
            <td><span data-field="tax_rate_0_1">{{ tax_rate_0_1 }}</span></td>
            <td>$0</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>2,050</td>
            <td><span data-field="tax_rate_2050_1">{{ tax_rate_2050_1 }}</span></td>
            <td>$307.50 + 25%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>4,850</td>
            <td><span data-field="tax_rate_4850_1">{{ tax_rate_4850_1 }}</span></td>
            <td>$1,007.50 + 28%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>7,400</td>
            <td><span data-field="tax_rate_7400_1">{{ tax_rate_7400_1 }}</span></td>
            <td>$1,721.50 + 33%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>10,050</td>
            <td><span data-field="tax_rate_10050_1">{{ tax_rate_10050_1 }}</span></td>
            <td>$2,596.00 + 35%</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <table style="font-size: 10pt;">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th style="width: 30%;">Of the amount over-</th>
            <th style="width: 70%;"></th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>0</td>
            <td>$0</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>2,050</td>
            <td>$0.25</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>4,850</td>
            <td>$0.28</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>7,400</td>
            <td>$0.33</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>10,050</td>
            <td>$0.35</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title" style="margin-top: 30px;">Record of Estimated Tax Payments</div>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 10%;">Pay- ment No.</th>
        <th style="width: 20%;">Date</th>
        <th style="width: 20%;">Check or money order number</th>
        <th style="width: 20%;">Amount</th>
        <th style="width: 30%;">2005 overpayment credit applied</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for i in range(1, 5) %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ i }}</td>
        <td><span data-field="payment_date_{{ i }}">{{ payment_date_i }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="payment_check_number_{{ i }}">{{ payment_check_number_i }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="payment_amount_{{ i }}">{{ payment_amount_i }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="overpayment_credit_{{ i }}">{{ overpayment_credit_i }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
      <tr>
        <td colspan="4">Total</td>
        <td><span data-field="total_overpayment_credit">{{ total_overpayment_credit }}</span></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 48%; border-top: 1px solid #000; padding-top: 5px;">Tear off here</div>
  </div>

</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div>
      <div style="font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold;">Form 1041-ES</div>
      <div style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Estimated Income Tax for Estates and Trusts</div>
      <div style="font-size: 10pt;">OMB No. 15-045-0971</div>
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: right;">
      <div style="font-size: 24pt; font-weight: bold;">2006</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Fiscal year filers-enter year ending</div>
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 10px;">
    <div>
      <div style="font-weight: bold;">Name of estate or trust</div>
      <div class="small-text"><span data-field="filer_name">{{ filer_name }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div style="font-weight: bold;">Type or print</div>
      <div class="small-text"><span data-field="filer_type">{{ filer_type }}</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Calendar year-Due Jan. 18, 2007</div>
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 10px;">
    <div>
      <div style="font-weight: bold;">Name of estate or trust</div>
      <div class="small-text"><span data-field="calendar_filer_name">{{ calendar_filer_name }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div style="font-weight: bold;">Amount of estimated tax you are paying by check or money order.</div>
      <div class="small-text">Dollars: <span data-field="calendar_amount_dollars">{{ calendar_amount_dollars }}</span> Cents: <span data-field="calendar_amount_cents">{{ calendar_amount_cents }}</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Calendar year-Due Sept. 15, 2007</div>
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 10px;">
    <div>
      <div style="font-weight: bold;">Name of estate or trust</div>
      <div class="small-text"><span data-field="calendar_filer_name_2">{{ calendar_filer_name_2 }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div style="font-weight: bold;">Amount of estimated tax you are paying by check or money order.</div>
      <div class="small-text">Dollars: <span data-field="calendar_amount_dollars_2">{{ calendar_amount_dollars_2 }}</span> Cents: <span data-field="calendar_amount_cents_2">{{ calendar_amount_cents_2 }}</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Calendar year-Due April 17, 2008</div>
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 10px;">
    <div>
      <div style="font-weight: bold;">Name of estate or trust</div>
      <div class="small-text"><span data-field="calendar_filer_name_3">{{ calendar_filer_name_3 }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div style="font-weight: bold;">Amount of estimated tax you are paying by check or money order.</div>
      <div class="small-text">Dollars: <span data-field="calendar_amount_dollars_3">{{ calendar_amount_dollars_3 }}</span> Cents: <span data-field="calendar_amount_cents_3">{{ calendar_amount_cents_3 }}</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Employer identification number</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="ein">{{ ein }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">Name of estate or trust</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="filer_name_2">{{ filer_name_2 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">Name and title of fiduciary</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="fiduciary_name">{{ fiduciary_name }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">Address of fiduciary (number, street, and room or suite no.)</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="fiduciary_address">{{ fiduciary_address }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">City, state, and ZIP code</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="fiduciary_city_state_zip">{{ fiduciary_city_state_zip }}</span></div>

</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div>
      <div style="font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold;">Form 1041-ES</div>
      <div style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">Estimated Income Tax for Estates and Trusts</div>
      <div style="font-size: 10pt;">OMB No. 15-045-0971</div>
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: right;">
      <div style="font-size: 24pt; font-weight: bold;">2006</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">2006 Tax Computation Worksheet Using Maximum Capital Gains Rates</div>
  <div class="small-text">
    Use this computation worksheet if the estate or trust expects a net capital gain or qualified dividends and line 6 of the 2006 Estimated Tax Worksheet is more than zero.
  </div>
  <div class="small-text" style="margin-top: 10px;">
    Caution: Do not include any amounts allocable to the beneficiaries of the estate or trust on lines 2, 3, and 4 below.
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">1. Enter taxable income (from line 5 of the 2006 Estimated Tax Worksheet)</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line1">{{ comp_line1 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">2. Enter the qualified dividends and net capital gain from the disposition of property held for investment that you elect to include in investment income.</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line2">{{ comp_line2 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">3. Enter the taxable income from line 1 minus line 2.</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line3">{{ comp_line3 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">4. Enter the unrecaptured section 1250 gain expected for 2006.</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line4">{{ comp_line4 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">5. Add lines 3 and 4 and enter the smaller of that sum or the amount of net capital gain from line 2.</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line5">{{ comp_line5 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">6. Subtract line 5 from line 2. If zero or less, enter -0</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line6">{{ comp_line6 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">7. Enter the smaller of line 1 or line 2.</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line7">{{ comp_line7 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">8. Enter the smaller of line 7 or line 8.</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line8">{{ comp_line8 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">9. Subtract line 8 from line 7. If zero or less, enter -0</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line9">{{ comp_line9 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">10. Tax on amount on line 11 from the 2006 Tax Rate Schedule</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line10">{{ comp_line10 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">11. Enter the amount from line 15</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line11">{{ comp_line11 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">12. Multiply line 15 by 5% (0.05)</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line12">{{ comp_line12 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">13. Add lines 11 and 12</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line13">{{ comp_line13 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">14. Enter the smaller of line 11 or line 13</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line14">{{ comp_line14 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">15. Subtract line 14 from line 13</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line15">{{ comp_line15 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">16. Multiply line 15 by 15% (0.15)</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line16">{{ comp_line16 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">17. Add lines 16 and 17</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line17">{{ comp_line17 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">18. Enter the smaller of line 17 or line 18</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line18">{{ comp_line18 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">19. Subtract line 18 from line 17</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line19">{{ comp_line19 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">20. Multiply line 19 by 15% (0.15)</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line20">{{ comp_line20 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">21. Add lines 20 and 21</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line21">{{ comp_line21 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">22. Enter the smaller of line 21 or line 22</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line22">{{ comp_line22 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">23. Subtract line 22 from line 21. If zero or less, enter -0</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line23">{{ comp_line23 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">24. Multiply line 23 by 25% (0.25)</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line24">{{ comp_line24 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">25. Add lines 24 and 25</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line25">{{ comp_line25 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">26. Multiply line 25 by 25% (0.25)</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line26">{{ comp_line26 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">27. Enter the amount from line 1</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line27">{{ comp_line27 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">28. Add lines 11, 15, 19, and 25</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line28">{{ comp_line28 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">29. Subtract line 28 from line 27</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line29">{{ comp_line29 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">30. Add lines 12, 16, 20, 26, and 30</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line30">{{ comp_line30 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">31. Tax. Enter the smaller of line 31 or line 32 here and on line 7 of the Worksheet on page 3.</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="comp_line31">{{ comp_line31 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">Exemption Worksheet for Qualified Distributions Only</div>
  <div class="small-text">
    If the estate or trust expects a net capital gain or qualified dividends and line 6 of the 2006 Estimated Tax Worksheet is more than zero, complete the worksheet below to figure the trust's exemption.
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">1. Maximum exemption</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="exemption_max">{{ exemption_max }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">2. Trust's adjusted gross income</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="exemption_agi">{{ exemption_agi }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">3. Subtract line 3 from line 2.</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="exemption_sub_agi">{{ exemption_sub_agi }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">4. Subtract line 4 from line 2. The result is not a whole number, increase it to the next higher whole number.</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="exemption_sub_4">{{ exemption_sub_4 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">5. Multiply line 5 by 2% (0.02) and enter the result as a decimal</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="exemption_mult_5">{{ exemption_mult_5 }}</span></div>

  <div class="section-title">6. Subtract line 7 from line 1. Enter the result here and line 4 of the 2006 Estimated Tax Worksheet on page 3.</div>
  <div class="small-text"><span data-field="exemption_final">{{ exemption_final }}</span></div>

</div>

